{"title":"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(parametric_plot)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (parametric plot)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amanda Reckonwith draws five circles with radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee053d9a8e7ad423615a57686481ea4bcf4cc28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then for each circle she plots the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e960acdcdd31f194b058e2abb368d5f9f76d47a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(C,A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />,\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is its circumference and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is its area. Which of the\nfollowing could be her graph?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5441a586e3c38f07d4057cb9867265ca14fdeb6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,2) , B= (3,4) , C= (4.5,7) , D= (6,11) , E= (7.5,16) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230f178f3cd06089682b3fe4a6a9ecf9580ef492.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,9) , B= (3,6) , C= (4.5,6) , D= (6,9) , E= (7.5,15) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95defaa77d8b1dd10283c438752810174f3e6d94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,2) , B= (3,6) , C= (4.5,8) , D= (6,6) , E= (7.5,2) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d43329cbcfb1249b7fcf1fc15cd2b90bc666ef4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,2) , B= (3,5) , C= (4.5,8) , D= (6,11) , E= (7.5,14) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d2b3b4be42360bf68db966abbc090187b5cdb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,15) , B= (3,10) , C= (4.5,6) , D= (6,3) , E= (7.5,1) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The circumference of a circle is obtained by simply multiplying the radius by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. So, the C-coordinate (in this case, it is the x-coordinate) will increase at a steady rate. The area, however, is obtained by squaring the radius and multiplying it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Since squares do not increase in an evenly spaced arithmetic sequence, the increase in the A-coordinates (aka the y- coordinates) will be much more significant. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e461cc6b19dcfd9ec41c0d49d3975d601135358c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"44\" height=\"28\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5441a586e3c38f07d4057cb9867265ca14fdeb6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); pair A= (1.5,2) , B= (3,4) , C= (4.5,7) , D= (6,11) , E= (7.5,16) ; draw((0,-1)--(0,16)); draw((-1,0)--(16,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,8), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (8,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />.\n-RBANDA\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28parametric_plot.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(parametric_plot)\">Solution 2 (parametric plot)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (parametric plot)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we know that the formula for circumference of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be893198fae2e36c717688a669bb05b467b3d3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi r$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and for the area of a circle it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e89ed1c5456915b4e95e0c8a11257ac5ed3d32c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, any coordinate is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228b0208fffc1b6601428ed06e43877df152805f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\pi r, \\pi r^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />, notice that, in more similar terms, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507e64f35cd86ba057bb6036a8c94d6626e4761c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\pi t, \\pi t^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"21\" />, which is a parametric plot. So let:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb44da8929144bde5619ac141e3458d5759550a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[X(t)=2\\pi t\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3dc6ba71957e697551edbdfca8917d61ff3f2e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y(t) = \\pi t^2\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943c64fb2dc570d8977c84c676eea242bb5f1432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{X(t)}{2\\pi} = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"40\" />, thus letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a6780507564f5b61d0f6039a37e62718e027e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y(t)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd36047157c38a5e07d5ddc0ad7dd65d533870e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(t)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5894084ddde826a207c1f33f4ce9cffefcfd1f43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\pi (\\frac{x^2}{4\\pi^2})\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/01760e16f3f9f1d40c733f3abefd88cee5a8390c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{x^2}{4\\pi}\\]\" width=\"56\" height=\"39\" />\nSince the domain of the function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44df9cb6ce6f056c64c197a004b64fc4dd3a5aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, note that the function is always increasing quadratically. The only answer choice that fits this function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AW6BhCQ_ig8\">https://youtu.be/AW6BhCQ_ig8</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 8\">2007 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201631\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 233/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6913/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.981      1 -total\n 56.65%    7.354      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 41.62%    5.403      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9086:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201631 and revision id 290535. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}